x=by['thm-good-reduction-and-smooth-proper-base-change'];s=x['statement'];s=s[:s.index('The commissioned smooth-proper')]+r'''(e) [prime-to-residue-characteristic etale good reduction] Locally let R be a DVR, K its fraction field and k its residue field, A_K an abelian variety and ell a prime different from char k. Then A_K has good reduction over R if and only if inertia acts trivially on T_ell(A_K), equivalently on A_K[ell^v](K^sep) for every v≥1. This is the Neron-Ogg-Shafarevich criterion, proved by the finite-etale torsion, affine torsion-growth and Neron properness route supplied locally. For an abelian scheme model the finite etale schemes A[ell^v] commute with every base change and specialize over a strict henselization to the special geometric torsion, preserving rank ell^{2gv}. The coherent cohomology clauses above and this etale good-reduction clause are both retained; no all-degree smooth-proper etale cohomology theorem is claimed by this finite-torsion route.''';x['statement']=s;x['deps']+=[helpers[7]['id'],helpers[6]['id'],'def-arith-tate-module-and-inertia']
